1. A system comprising:  
a memory storing instructions and a customer sentiment score;  
a voice input interface configured to receive voice data representing speech of a customer; and  
at least one processor operatively coupled to the memory and the voice input interface, the at least one processor being configured, upon execution of the instructions, to:  
extract one or more voice-pattern features from the voice data;  
analyze the one or more voice-pattern features to determine a sentiment associated with the speech;  
generate the customer sentiment score based on the determined sentiment;  
update the customer sentiment score based on subsequently received voice data;  
determine an action based at least in part on the updated customer sentiment score; and  
cause the determined action to be performed.

### Exemplary Patent Specification Language

A computer-implemented contact-center system is configured to obtain customer data associated with a customer from a plurality of communication channels, including at least one voice channel and at least one non-voice channel. The customer data includes data associated with a current customer interaction and historical data associated with one or more prior customer interactions. During the current customer interaction, the system applies speech-analytics processing to audio data received through the voice channel to determine a sentiment score representative of a detected customer sentiment. The system dynamically updates the sentiment score as additional portions of the current customer interaction are received and analyzed. Based at least in part on the updated sentiment score and the historical customer data, the system generates and presents one or more recommended actions for handling the current customer interaction.

### Exemplary Independent Claim

1. **A computer-implemented method comprising:**

   retrieving, by a contact-center computing platform, customer data associated with a customer from a plurality of communication channels comprising a voice channel and a non-voice channel, the customer data comprising data associated with a current interaction and historical data associated with one or more previous interactions;

   receiving audio data corresponding to the current interaction conducted through the voice channel;

   applying a speech-analytics model to the audio data to generate a sentiment score indicative of a sentiment associated with the customer;

   updating the sentiment score during the current interaction in response to receiving and analyzing additional audio data;

   determining, based at least in part on the updated sentiment score and at least a portion of the historical data, a recommended action associated with the current interaction; and

   causing the recommended action to be presented to a contact-center agent or executed by the contact-center computing platform.

### Exemplary System Claim

2. **A contact-center system comprising:**

   one or more processors; and

   memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the contact-center system to:

   - aggregate current and historical customer data from voice and non-voice communication channels;
   - analyze speech received during a current customer interaction to determine a customer sentiment score;
   - repeatedly update the customer sentiment score as the current customer interaction progresses; and
   - select and output one or more recommended actions based on the updated customer sentiment score and the aggregated customer data.
